{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1547921-me-sharing-cults","id":1547921,"title":"Me sharing Cults","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-23T15:06:29-08:00","id":1547921,"title":"Me sharing Cults","content":"<b>De Genootschap van de Ongeziene Haard</b><br /> <br /> In the late 20th century, as the world grew more interconnected, alienation paradoxically spread like a shadow. In the face of this growing isolation, a small group of individuals came together, united by a shared sense of being &quot;out of place.&quot; Initially, they formed an informal support network for those feeling lost, alienated, or disconnected from the larger society. They offered solace to people grappling with social conflicts, cultural clashes. At first, their work was simple: providing emotional support, creating spaces where people could share their experiences, and forming a sense of belonging in a world that seemed to leave them behind.<br /> <br /> As the group grew, however, its leaders began to see that the greatest threat to their mission wasn\u2019t external opposition, but internal division. They realized that without a strong sense of unity, their movement risked becoming just another fragmented effort in a world already overflowing with them. The concept of unity became central to their vision: a unified society, not defined by external origin or background, but by shared values of trust, security, and understanding.<br /> <br /> The leaders came to understand that the strength of their vision lay in creating something that transcended borders and divisions. To that end, they envisioned a society of like-minded individuals. Today, there are few decentralized network of support groups scattered across the globe. These groups are varied in their form and focus \u2014 some serve as social networks for citizens who feel disconnected from their local communities, while others support students. There are even groups dedicated to psychological well-being, offering a space for those seeking to reconcile emotional turmoil or mental health struggles in a world that often feels isolating.<br /> <br /> The foundation of &quot;De Genootschap van de Ongeziene Haard&quot; lies in volunteering and supporting the local communities in which it operates, with members often dedicating their time and resources to outreach and care. In addition to offering a network of support, group also focus on training individuals in specialized practices and share advices.<br /> <br /> <b>Cultist:</b> travelers, individuals seeking a sense of belonging, union leaders, society activists, low ranked members of local government, philanthropist.<br /> <br /> 1st Degree <b>De Nieuwkomer: Zelfreflectie</b><br /> The initiate develops an acute ability to see themselves more clearly and understand motivations.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain Empathy specialty - Emotions, Motives.<br /> <br /> 2nd Degree <b>De Zoeker: Spiegelziel</b><br /> Through their journey in self-acceptance, the member learns to act as a &quot;mirror&quot; for others, reflecting their truths back at them.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain &quot;Empath&quot; (Hurt Locker)<br /> <br /> 3rd Degree <b>De Gids: Gezichtloze Waarheid</b><br /> The initiate has mastered the art of embracing and hiding their true identity. They understands both the complexities of their own identity and the struggles others face and so make choices knowing what can influence them.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain &quot;Common Sense&quot; merit.<br /> <br /> 4th Degree <b>De Raadgever: Schaduwzelf</b><br /> Having fully integrated their hidden and visible personas, the member got deeper understanding of inner emotional and mental processes; they can communicates with &quot;Shadow Self&quot; of others to confront their insecurities, emotions or desires.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain 3 dots in &quot;Peacemaker&quot; merit, ignore prerequisites. (Hurt Locker)<br /> <br /> 5th Degree <b>De Wijze: Volledig Zelf</b><br /> The highest-ranked members of the Society have achieved full harmony with their hidden and visible selves, becoming paragons of authenticity and influence. Their presence inspires others to reflect.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain the &quot;Inspiring&quot; merit for free, ignore prerequisites. Additionally, once per chapter, you may grant allies a +2 bonus on any rolls involving self-confidence, emotional resilience, or clarity of purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>Alternate Supernatural benefits:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Common Sense or Hunger Management; ignore prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Reconciler 3 or Peacemaker, if had both - gain 1 experience. <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>Harakternyky </b>[For Dark Eras, ~ 16-19 centuries]<br /> <br /> The Harakternyky were a legendary group of warrior-mystics, renowned for their supernatural resilience, mastery of combat, and uncanny ability to outwit their enemies. Their mystique grew as tales circulated of their invulnerability to bullets, their ability to walk on water, vanish into thin air, and even transform into animals.<br /> <br /> The cult's practices blended Christian faith with ancient Slavic magic, resulting in a unique spiritual tradition. Their members contact with otherworld \u2014 sometimes with divine forces, other times with darker powers \u2014 which grant them the &quot;character&quot; (\u0445\u0430\u0440\u0430\u043a\u0442\u0435\u0440) that made them impervious to harm.<br /> <br /> Initiates of the Harakternyky undergo rigorous physical and spiritual training, studying occult rites, survival techniques, and martial skills. As they progress through the ranks, they not only gain combat expertise but also master supernatural abilities that connect them to the mystical forces.<ul><li><b>Status Benefits:</b> Use half your Mystery Cult Status rating (rounded up) as a bonus or penalty when interacting with those who recognize your craft.</li> <li><b>Prerequisites:</b> After achieving the 2nd rank, the initiate must possess <i><b>equal </b></i>Professional Training rank in a military-related profession to progress further; skills such as <b>Weaponry</b>, <b>Firearms</b>, <b>Animal Ken</b>, <b>Survival</b>, or <b>Warfare</b>.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mythical Arsenal:</b> Biokinesis, Numbing Touch, Telekinesis, Apportation (buy rest with experience points). </div> </div> </div>1th Degree <b>Volotsyuha:</b> The initiate begins as an eager learner, traveling to gain survival skills and learn the basics of mysticism. They are taught to read the land, navigate dangers, and defend themselves with rudimentary martial techniques.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain a specialty in one of the following specialties - Survival (Steppe), Weaponry (Saber), Firearms (Pistol, Rifle) or Occult (Folk Magic).<br /> <br /> <br /> 2nd Degree <b>Dzhura:</b> They begin their deeper training in the occult arts, learning the first of the Harakternyk rites and learn healing techniques.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain Holistic Awareness and one of the following - Mythical Arsenal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After acquaring this rank, Harakternyk may perform occult rite to make a charm or enchant his weapon (Hurt Locker) and buy another Supernatural Merits. </div> </div> </div><br /> 3rd Degree <b>Zaklynach:</b> The Zaklynach is a seasoned warrior-mystic who has mastered both physical combat and the mystical arts. At this stage, they gain unparalleled focus in their chosen area of expertise and further access to supernatural abilities. The Zaklynach may also begin augmenting their body with magical resilience, becoming seemingly impervious to harm.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain Area of Expertise (cult specialty) and spend 2 dots among Mythical Arsenal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After acquaring this rank, baseline characters (with maximum rating in <b>Iron Skin</b>) may buy one dot in <b>Iron Skin (Advanced)</b>. </div> </div> </div><br /> 4th Degree <b>Mol\u2019far:</b> Mol\u2019fary are deeply connected to the forces of nature and the unseen, capable of channeling their power to heal allies, curse enemies, and shield their kin from harm.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Gain Laying on Hands; if had one - gain one experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> 5th Degree <b>Harakternyk:</b> These masters are blending myth and reality. They are invincible warriors, cunning strategists, and unmatched mystics who wield the full arsenal of Harakternyk abilities. Some say their souls are so deeply tied to the land that they can never truly die.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Distribute 3 dots between next: Mythical Arsenal.<br /> <br /> <b>Alternate Supernatural benefits:</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> World is full of monsters and unknown. It is hard to predict who will follow one road or another. These MCI was created for baseline humans with few notes for others. Whenever you deside to use templates that are not listed here - remember that most can't use Supernatural merits, replace those with merits, skills or specialties that reflect mastery in battle, survivability (often physical merits) or their knowledge of sorcery (be it merits or Gifts). If so happened character possesses all reasonable merits when you increase rating of these merit -&gt; gain one experience. </div> </div> </div><b>Beast:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022 Gain Holistic Awareness and either Trained Observer or Hunger Management.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Iron Skin (\u2022\u2022) [BtP version - maximum rating] and dot in Fast Reflexes. If Beast had maximum rating in one of those merits - upgrade it to Advanced / Epic.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain one Nightmare related to spirits, ghosts or witches, even without Family Tie.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Kinship merits with spirits, ghosts or witches. Beast keep those merits even if it never had or lost such kinship. Beast may change those merits by Sanctity of Merits after making relevant Family Ties.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022 Gain Holistic Awareness and another related specialty.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain one Ceremony.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain 3 dots in Retribution.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Haunt (Affinity) or Ceremony and Occult specialty.<br /> <br /> <b>Kindred:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022 Gain Holistic Awareness and dot in Fighting merit.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Area of Expertise and 2 dots in Fighting merits.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Bloodhound merit.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain 3 dots in Physical or Fighting merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b><br /> \u2022\u2022 Choose from the next list: Fast Spells or Quick Draw and Fighting merit.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Nameless may choose 3 skills as rote skills: Survival, Occult, Weaponry, Firearms.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Non-nameless mages gain 3 dots in Fighting merits.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Astral Adept or gain 1 experience.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain Astral Intruder or Potent Soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b><br /> Replace Mythical Arsenal and Laying on Hands with Affinity Gift or Physical/Fighting merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon:</b><br /> Unchained can not show up near people without the risk of ruining their cover. Replace all Supernatural merits with Fighting merits and Embeds which could create a Fame of a sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 02-24-2025, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}